; SkoolKit expands no PageContent on a page with a SectionPrefix, so the notes
; below are an [Audio:...] entry too.
[Page:Sound]
SectionPrefix=Audio

[Audio:clips:About these clips]
Every sound effect below drives the loudspeaker through #R$B9B4(one square-wave routine), and every tune
through #R$D568(the tune player). The bursts and their order come from the code. The gaps between them are estimates,
because the game paces itself.

[Audio:title_tune:Title tune]
The tune heard on the title screen, in the high-score wait, and while the game-over screen waits for a restart. Fed byte by byte to #R$D568(the tune player) from #R$D642(its note data).

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=36207,stop=35775,vol=25)(title_tune.wav)

[Audio:game_over_tune:Game-over tune]
The tune that marks the end of a game. Fed byte by byte to #R$D568(the tune player) from #R$D605(its note data).

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=36174,stop=36195,vol=25)(game_over_tune.wav)

[Audio:key_press_blip:Key-press blip]
The blip that answers a key press in the menus and prompts, and when you pause or resume. Played by #R$B77C(the key-press blip routine).

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(key_press_blip.wav)(#INCLUDE(PlaySoundDelays))

[Audio:ball_bounce:Ball bounce]
The ball as it comes off the bat. Played by #R$B898.

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47256,stop=47270,vol=25)(ball_bounce.wav)

[Audio:brick_hit:Brick hit]
The blip when the missile shot breaks a brick. Played by #R$B8A7(the brick-hit sound routine).

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47271,stop=47286,vol=25)(brick_hit.wav)

[Audio:brick_destroyed:Brick destroyed]
A brick hit that shatters the brick to an empty slot. Played by #R$B8B7(the brick-destroyed sound routine).

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47287,stop=47323,vol=25)(brick_destroyed.wav)

[Audio:brick_survives:Brick survives the hit]
A brick hit that leaves the brick in place: a golden brick, or a silver brick
that steps down. Played by #R$B8DC.

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47324,stop=47339,vol=25)(brick_survives.wav)

[Audio:prize_reveal_tune:Prize-reveal tune]
Four notes, played when a ball reveals a prize. Fed byte by byte to #R$D568(the tune player) from
#R$D743(its note data).

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(prize_reveal_tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(PrizeRevealTuneDelays))

[Audio:bomb_detonate:Bomb detonation]
The bomb prize as it blows its 3×3 hole in the field. Played by #R$B8EC(the bomb sound routine).

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(bomb_detonate.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopDDelays))

[Audio:bat_grows:Bat grows]
The bat as it grows longer when the expand prize is taken. Played by #R$B92A(the bat-grows sound routine).

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(bat_grows.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopEDelays))

[Audio:bat_shrinks:Bat shrinks]
The expanded bat as it shrinks back to its normal size. Played by #R$B968.

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(bat_shrinks.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopFDelays))

[Audio:safety_net_flash:Safety net flash]
The safety net barrier as it flashes. Played by #R$B991.

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(safety_net_flash.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopGDelays))

[Audio:inhabitant_spawns:Inhabitant spawns]
An inhabitant as it spawns. Played by #R$B7DF(the spawn sound routine).

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(inhabitant_spawns.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopBDelays))

[Audio:death_burst:Death burst]
The death burst, as an inhabitant dies or the bat explodes when the last ball in
play is lost. A missile shot that bursts on a wall and a ball gem whose flight runs
out play it too. Played by #R$B7AE.

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(death_burst.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopADelays))

[Audio:second_ball_spawn:Second-ball spawn]
Ball B as it spawns. Played by #R$B78F.

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=46991,stop=47002,vol=25)(second_ball_spawn.wav)

[Audio:chew:Orb chews the ball]
The orb as it works the ball in its mouth. Played by #R$B836.

#AUDIO(0,vol=25)(chew.wav)(#INCLUDE(LoopCDelays))

[Audio:orb_spit:Orb spits the ball out]
The upward sweep when the orb spits the ball out. Played by #R$B884.

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47236,stop=47255,vol=25)(orb_spit.wav)

[Audio:menu_move:Name-entry cursor move]
The cursor as it steps along the name-entry strip. Every position on the strip has
its own pitch. Played by #R$B85A.

#AUDIO(sim=1,start=47194,stop=47218,vol=25)(menu_move.wav)

